    "narrative": "The focal point of today\u2019s lineup is **Corbin Carroll**, who commands an elite score of 87.14. Facing the soft-tossing Mikolas, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive park boost and the rare opportunity to exploit a slow pitcher delivery, which drastically increases his stolen base upside\u2014our scarcest and most coveted category. Similarly, **James Wood** (69.70) remains a lock due to his elite xwOBA (.423) and leadoff placement. Both **Gabriel Moreno** (70.58) and **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) project strongly against the high xERA of the opposing rotation, with **Gabriel Moreno**\u2019s recency and **Isaac Paredes**'s platoon advantage against a righty like Fedde providing the necessary floor to cement them in the starting spots.\n\nThe decision to bench **Seiya Suzuki** (46.99) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he holds a respectable projection, the combination of a tough matchup against Ashcraft and a marginal park factor pushed his efficiency below the established threshold of our deeper, more advantageous plays like **Henry Bolte** (47.99), who earns the nod primarily due to his lower-order platoon efficiency. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Jose Caballero** (48.26); while his status is technically \"Lineup Pending,\" the heavy penalty associated with facing an elite arm like S\u00e1nchez\u2014compounded by the catcher\u2019s hold time and the pitcher\u2019s stingy reputation for suppressing base-stealing attempts\u2014makes him a high-risk, low-reward play today. \n\nWe are monitoring the **Jose Caballero** situation closely, as any shift in his batting order could further dampen his outlook. Conversely, **Josh Naylor** (49.91) remains a volatile start while staring down deGrom; he only avoids the bench because his base projection holds up despite the massive SP skill penalty. We are keeping **Travis Bazzana** (36.57) and **Cole Young** (39.16) safely on the bench to preserve our game caps, as neither reaches the required floor for a daily start. With **Vinnie Pasquantino** confirmed out of the lineup, our bench depth is intentionally thin, focusing exclusively on maximizing the efficiency of the active starters in pursuit of those crucial stolen base points.",
